wn  conclusions is there the possibility as  russia faces ukrainian resistance  supported by the us  that there could be airstrikes here in  poland where the munitions the missiles  the weaponry is landing and going to  ukraine  if there is and russia has declared war  on nato and nato will fight back we've  spoken to members of congress who  described the situation that they've  seen here on the border and also in  ukraine  in terms that evoke world war ii  poland in 1939.  do you think those are fair  if you look at the pictures coming out  of harkev if you look at the pictures  coming out of mariupol where civilians  are trying to flee and russia is  stopping them shooting them on the  street if they try to leave  i think that it certainly uh has some  similarities to those other tragedies  that's saying a lot  how does this end  i don't know how it ends i hope it ends  by the ukrainians being victorious and i  think ultimately it will end by the  ukrainians being victorious hopefully  sooner and hopefully uh with fewer  casualties but anyway it ends the  ukrainians will not let russia occupy it  the ukrainians will fight they're  fighting now and they will continue to  fight and i am convinced that the  ukrainians will ultimately win  i know tony i was wondering that very  same question how does it end if the  bombing continues and people leave their  homes what is left of ukraine what does  putin really have at the end of the day  it's a good question gail one of the  great fears i think everybody watching  this from the outside as well as the  people in ukraine have  is putin may win militarily but if he  tries to then occupy how long could this  fight last a very long time indeed and  that is the worry and i want to add a  detail to why we're seeing so many  people over the border still coming in  over my shoulder and those are new  people those buses leave every 15  minutes or so full to the brim and then  a new crowd arrives the reason they're  here coming 